[Music]  the riddler is one of the most famous  villains in all of comic book history  second perhaps only to the joker since  first appearing in an october 1948 issue  of detective comics edward enigma has  continuously proven to be one of  batman's most challenging foes known for  his love of crime drama and of course  one singularly puzzling punctuation mark  the riddler has appeared in nearly as  many mediums as the batman himself in  addition to his long history in the  comic books the riddler has also made a  number of memorable appearances in  animated form most animated riddler fans  are likely familiar with john glover's  iteration of the character from 1992's  batman the animated series but glover's  animated version of the character is  actually only one of many the first  animated riddler appeared in a 1968 cbs  tv series titled the batman superman  hour in his first animated incarnation  the famous villain is voiced by actor  ted knight and since the riddler's debut  in animation he has been voiced by no  less than 14 different actors of course  most people are probably more familiar  with the various live-action adaptations  of the character in the 1960s nigma was  played by two actors the adams family  star john astin played the character in  the second season of adam west's batman  tv series however the actor who arguably  made the character famous was frank  gorshin whose portrayal of the character  in seasons 1 and 3 of the show is still  considered one of the best versions of  the character ever gorham's riddler was  so beloved by audiences and critics that  the actor was nominated for an emmy a  first for the batman franchise gorshin  would also go on to reprise his role as  the riddler in the 1966 film of the same  name and in the years since the  riddler's fame has only grown many  millennials probably first came to know  the character as a result of jim  carrey's role in 1995's batman forever  though that film isn't beloved by many  carrie's campy performance is often  noted as a highlight of the movie  now  that's impressive  modern tv audiences may be more familiar  with corey michael smith's take on  enigma from the 2014 fox series gotham  matt reeves the batman is also set to  tackle a new incarnation of the infamous  character according to a recent  interview with reeves this version of  the riddler is actually named edward  nashton and is loosely based on the  zodiac killer so who is the next actor  set to bring him to life emmy  award-nominated actor paul dano will  portray the infamous villain in robert  pattinson's first outing as the caped  crusader since dano's casting was first  announced in october 2019 dano has  maintained the usual vow of silence  against spoilers but he's also been  willing to offer a few teases about his  unique take on the character in a recent  interview with empire magazine dano  called his costume intense and powerful  if you recognize dano that's because  he's been a working actor since the late  1990s in fact daniel's relationship with  warner brothers goes all the way back to  his first on-screen appearance in a 1998  episode of smart guy in the early years  of his career dano established himself  with a handful of small rules including  two minor appearances on the sopranos  while dano has worked on a few  television series including an emmy  nominated role on showtime's escape at  dannemora the majority of the actors  work has been on the big screen many  audiences first became aware of dano for  his role in 2006's little miss sunshine  but his portrayal of paul and eli sunday  in 2007's there will be blood may have  been what rocketed the young actor to  the a-list for his work in the film dana  was nominated for a bafta award for best  supporting actor in the years since  daniel has also appeared in movies as  varied as prisoners love and mercy and  swiss army men you can get a full look  at daniel's riddler when the batman hits  theaters on march 4th  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

